-- title:
--   Fibres of the fine family over geometric points
-- statement:
--   The setting is the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation package for fake elliptic curves, with an enormous list of data and hypotheses; they are introduced here group by group, each group named by its Lean binders, and several groups are summarised as indicated.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with `hrr` : $\bar r\neq r$, and a non-zero level $N$ with `hrN`, `hrbarN` : $r\nmid N$, $\bar r\nmid N$ and `hN` : $N$ squarefree.
--
--   **The base ring.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which by `hdvr` is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi$ is an irreducible element (`hπ`), $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and `hunr` : $(r)=(\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **The unramified cover.** $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is a characteristic-zero domain over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $F_r$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal being maximal (`hOnr_max`); `hOnr_alg` requires every element of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ to satisfy a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ whose value at the element lies in $(\pi)$, `hOnr_closed` requires every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ to have a root modulo $(\pi)$, and `hFr` : $F_r x\equiv x^{r}\pmod{(\pi)}$ for all $x$.
--
--   **The determinant valuation.** $v_{\det}$ is a homomorphism $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $v_{\det}(g)$ is $n$ exactly when $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **The indefinite quaternion algebra and its moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ with `hB` : $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ has $0<a$ or $0<b$ and is locally a division algebra exactly at the places above $r$ and $\bar r$; $\Lambda$ is a maximal order (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with structure map $f$ and a point rule `pt` on fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level $N$ is a coarse moduli space (`h𝒳` : `IsCoarseModuli`, i.e. invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullback, bijectivity of the point rule on algebraically closed fields modulo isomorphism, and the universal property).
--
--   **The fine moduli space with full level $n$ and the twisting group.** An integer $n\ge 3$ (`hn`) with $r\nmid n$, $\bar r\nmid n$ (`hrn`, `hrbarn`) and $\gcd(n,N)=1$ (`hnN`); $M\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point rule `ptF` on pairs (curve, full level-$n$ structure) is a fine moduli space (`hM`); a group $G$ with $\rho:G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ and labels $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ satisfying `hρ` : `IsLevelTwistAction` ($\rho$ acts over the base, the automorphism $\rho(g)$ realises twisting the level structure by $\chi(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n$ in the precise sense of that structure). The forgetful morphism $p:M\to\mathcal X$ lies over the base (`hp`), is $G$-invariant (`hρp`) and is compatible with the two point rules (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **Hecke and Atkin–Lehner structure on $\mathcal X$.** For every prime $\ell\neq r,\bar r$, a coarse moduli space $\mathcal Y_\ell\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ for curves with extra $\ell$-level (`h𝒴`) together with two projections $d_0,d_1$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) realising on points the forgetful map (`hd₀`) and the passage to an $\ell$-isogenous quotient (`hd₁`); self-maps $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **The definite quaternion side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `hdef` : $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ locally a division algebra exactly at the places above $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`) containing (`hRΛ₁`) an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (`hR₁`); an idele $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that the intersection order $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0:\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); and the place $v$ above $r$ (`hv`).
--
--   **The arithmetic group and Hecke elements.** $\tilde\Gamma=$ `Γt` is, by `hΓt`, the group of units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ integral for $R_1$ at every place other than $v$. For each prime $\ell\neq r,\bar r$ there are $s_\ell$ and an idele $s^{f}_\ell$ whose local components agree with $s_\ell$ away from $r$ and are trivial at $r$, such that the diagonal idele of $\ell$ times $(s^f_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ and $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of that order at $\ell$ otherwise, and with $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$ (`hs`); `hΓtℓ` defines $\tilde\Gamma_\ell=\tilde\Gamma\cap s_\ell\tilde\Gamma s_\ell^{-1}$. An element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\tilde\Gamma$ is given by `hwbar`.
--
--   **Coordinates on $\Lambda$.** `hΛℤ` : every integer lies in $\Lambda$; `coord` sends $\Lambda$ to pairs of elements of the Witt ring $\mathbb W(\mathbb F_{r^2})$ and satisfies `IsOrderCoord` (`hcoord`): additivity, normalisation at $1$, the twisted multiplication rule, injectivity, $r$-adic density and the trace condition.
--
--   **The special fibre.** $A_0$ is a fake elliptic curve over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$, $X_0$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of height $4$ (`hX₀`), $\theta_0$ a system of formal coordinates of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and `hA₀` asserts that $A_0$ is a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$; $e,e':\tilde\Gamma\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees `deg`.
--
--   **The uniformisation package on the special fibre** (the hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4`, together with the order $R_2\le R_1$ with `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`, the extension $\hat e$ of $e$ to $R_2$ with `hê` and the clauses `hE5a`, `hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`, `hE5c`, `hE5d`, `hE5e`; summarised here): $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the $N$-level; $\gamma\mapsto e\gamma$ is multiplicative and sends rational scalars to scalars, up to multiplication by powers of $r$, and only scalars act by scalars; every injective embedding of the centraliser of the $\mathcal O_D$-action and $\varpi$ on $X_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ matches, after conjugation by a single $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ and up to powers of $r$, the endomorphism of $X_0$ inducing $e\gamma$ with $\iota_0(\gamma)$; full level-$n$ structures on $A_0$ are permuted by $e$ according to labels in $\Lambda$ which are multiplicative modulo $n$; every $r$-power self-isogeny pair preserving the level of a fake elliptic curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ up to powers of $r$; and $\hat e$ is an additive, $\Lambda$-equivariant, level-preserving, unital, multiplicative extension to $R_2$ compatible with integers, with reduced norms, with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\tilde\Gamma$, and with the same simultaneous matrix realisation as in `hE2`.
--
--   **The special formal module and its moduli package.** A ring map $\iota:\mathbb W(\mathbb F_{r^2})\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$; $\Phi$ a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a rule $\eta$ turning rigidified objects into points of $MD$, with `hη` (three clauses: on admissible objects $\eta$ identifies points exactly for isomorphic objects, $\eta$ is natural in the base ring, and every point of $MD$ is, after a finite covering family of localisations spanning the unit ideal, in the image of $\eta$ on admissible objects); and an injective embedding $E_0$ of the centraliser of the $\mathcal O_D$-action and $\varpi$ on $\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the precise sense of `hE₀`.
--
--   **The Drinfeld comparison.** A family of maps `eD` from the $G$-points of $MD$ to pairs (an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$, a Deligne datum over $B$) for noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, natural in $B$ (`hnatD`), bijective (`hbijD`), preserving the first coordinate (`hfstD`), turning the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on $MD$-points into `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` (`hGLD`) and $\varpi$-translation into the Frobenius twist $F_r^{1}$ on the first coordinate (`hPiD`), with $\varpi$-translates always existing (`hPiexD`).
--
--   **Transport between the two special fibres.** A ring map $\kappa:O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ with `hκ`, an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which by `hβ₀` is an isogeny $\Phi\to\kappa_*X_0$ of height $4n_0$; and $P_0$ a full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ on the special fibre.** A curve $A_{0w}$, maps $a_w,a_w'$ exhibiting it as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), maps $b_w,b_w'$ forming an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ which preserves the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw`, which requires, for every injective embedding as in `hE2`, a single conjugating $g$ realising simultaneously the $\tilde\Gamma$-family and the composite $a_w\!\gg\! b_w$, the latter matching $\iota_0(\bar w)$ up to a power of $r$.
--
--   **The period map $\Xi$.** For noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, $\Xi$ assigns a $G$-point of $MD$ to every rigidified curve; `hΞleg` says that over connected $B$ the associated map $O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$, `hΞnat` that $\Xi$ is compatible with pullback of rigidified curves, `hΞiso` that $\Xi$ is unchanged under isomorphisms of rigidified curves in the stated sense, and `hΞdef` gives the explicit description of $\Xi$ through a rigidified object $t$ with $j\le 1$, `IsRigTransport` with respect to $\theta_0,\kappa,\beta_0$, admissibility for the $(-j)$-twist, and $\Xi=\langle F_r^{-j}\psi,\eta(t)\rangle$.
--
--   **Compatibilities with the group actions.** An element $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$; `heqΓ` : over connected $B$, translating a rigidification by $e\gamma$ corresponds, for some $c\in\mathbb Z$, to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ on the $\Xi$-images; `heqW` : the same for the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ with $\iota_0(\bar w)$, under the stated comparison of rigidifications.
--
--   **The normalised leg.** Writing $\psi^{\natural}=F_r^{-v_{\det}(g_0)}\psi$, the clauses `hK1`–`hK4` state: every Deligne datum over a connected $B$ is realised by a curve with a $\psi^{\natural}$-rigidification whose $\Xi$-image has first coordinate $\psi^{\natural}$ and is $g_0^{-1}$-twisted-equivalent to $(\psi,P)$ (`hK1`); two such realisations are isomorphic, compatibly with the rigidifications (`hK2`); they pull back along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps (`hK3`); and they descend along a surjection whose kernel has square zero in the stated sense (`hK4`). Clauses `hC0e`, `hC0u` assert existence and uniqueness of the normalised level-$n$ structure transported from $P_0$ along a rigidification.
--
--   **The fine family $\Theta_f$.** For noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, $\Theta_f$ sends a triple (an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi$, a Deligne datum $P$, an element of $G$) to a $B$-point of $M$ over the base, naturally in $B$ (`hnat`); `hG` : $\Theta_f(x,gh)$ followed by $\rho(h)$ equals $\Theta_f(x,g)$; `hC2` : $\Theta_f((\psi,P),1)$ is the fine moduli point of the pair (curve, transported level-$n$ structure) attached to a normalised rigidification with datum $P$; `hC2c` : its composite with $p$ is the coarse moduli point of that curve. Finally $\theta_t:\tilde\Gamma\to G$ is a group homomorphism, `hC3` is the translation clause (translating the datum by $\iota_0(\gamma)$ produces a second normalised rigidification of the same curve, whose transported level-$n$ structure is the $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$-twist of the first, and whose extra $\ell$-level subgroups, for primes $\ell\neq r$ invertible in $B$, match those transported through $e\gamma$), and `hC5` is the one-leg fibre clause over algebraically closed fields: two normalised rigidified curves with data $P,P'$ and an isomorphism of the underlying curves give a $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ carrying $(\psi,P)$ to $(\psi,P')$ under the twisted action, matching transported level-$n$ structures through the isomorphism after twisting by $\chi(\theta_t\gamma)$, and matching extra $\ell$-level subgroups with those preserved by $e\gamma$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent in $k$, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi:O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to k$, all Deligne data $P,P'$ over $k$ and all $g,g'\in G$:
--   $$\Theta_f\big((\psi,P),g\big)=\Theta_f\big((\psi,P'),g'\big)$$
--   holds if and only if there exists $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ such that both
--
--   (i) $g'=\theta_t(\gamma)\,g$ in $G$, and
--
--   (ii) $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ are related by the twisted action of the image of $\gamma$ under $\iota_0$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, that is: $\psi=F_r^{-v_{\det}(\iota_0\gamma)}\psi$, and for every full lattice $M$ in $K_0^2$ the line of $P'$ at $M$ is the preimage, under the base-changed isomorphism induced by $(\iota_0\gamma)^{-1}$, of the line of $P$ at the lattice $(\iota_0\gamma)^{-1}M$.
--
--   This is the fibre computation for the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation of the fine moduli space of fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure: over an algebraically closed base in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, the family $\Theta_f$ on $(O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-structure, Deligne datum, $G$-label$)$ identifies two triples exactly when they lie in one orbit of the arithmetic group $\tilde\Gamma$ acting through $\theta_t$ on the $G$-coordinate and through $\iota_0$ on the $p$-adic upper half plane coordinate. It is the geometric-point input to the companion one-leg statement [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_eq_iff_exists_mem_levelHom_of_isAlgClosed_heightNormalised_eq_hC5oneLeg`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.fineFamily_eq_iff_exists_mem_levelHom_of_isAlgClosed_heightNormalised_eq_hC5oneLeg), and thence to the construction of the uniformisation isomorphism used in the study of reduction of Shimura curves.
